@* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   PROJECT-ROOT component imports.

   Razor merges _Imports.razor files from the project root downwards, so this file applies to
   EVERY .razor in the project, while Components/_Imports.razor continues to layer the DNN
   component namespaces on top for the Components/ subtree only.

   This file exists because the converted .ascx components live under admin/ and
   DesktopModules/, which are NOT under Components/ and therefore inherited none of the
   framework usings. The symptoms were all the same missing-using root cause:
     * CS1660 "cannot convert lambda expression to type 'bool'" on every
       @onchange="@(e => ...)" handler - ChangeEventArgs was unresolved, so the compiler fell
       back to a non-delegate overload (28 occurrences across admin/Modules, admin/Tabs).
     * CS0103 "the name 'InteractiveServer' does not exist" on @rendermode directives.
     * CS1061 "IJSRuntime does not contain a definition for 'InvokeVoidAsync'" - that is an
       extension method in Microsoft.JSInterop.JSRuntimeExtensions.

   DELIBERATELY FRAMEWORK-ONLY. Do NOT add DNN component namespaces here. Several component
   type names are duplicated across DNN namespaces (User, Text, Copyright, Help, Login, Terms,
   Privacy, Message, Settings, ViewProfile), and bringing two of them into one scope produces
   RZ9985 "multiple components use the tag '<X>'". Those components are addressed either by
   fully-qualified tag name or through IDnnControlTypeResolver, which is why the per-directory
   _Imports files and per-file @using directives stay as they are.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *@

@using System
@using System.Collections.Generic
@using System.Linq
@using System.Threading.Tasks

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Sections
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.RenderMode

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http
@using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
